WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
Press two fingers to your wrist.

2
00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.500
There it is: your pulse.

3
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.570
Now imagine it going for a whole lifetime.

4
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.510
Nobody counts every beat.

5
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.470
A physicist doesn't need to.

6
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.110
You break the problem into small
factors you can estimate, then multiply.

7
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.970
So roughly how many beats is that?

8
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:19.890
A million?

9
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:20.860
A billion?

10
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.250
Or a trillion?

11
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.500
In this mission, you'll learn
what an order of magnitude is,

12
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.920
and where the cut-off between
two powers of ten sits.

13
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.410
Then you'll learn numbers worth knowing,
from the width of an atom to the radius

14
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.580
of Earth.

15
00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.880
Your mission: estimate a
lifetime of heartbeats,

16
00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.550
to the nearest power of ten.
